# Observe the return path for a control boomerang and the Dwarven Thrower.
#
# WHAT IS BEING MEASURED. A returning thrown weapon prints "<item> returns to
# you." at src/Fight.cpp:1089. A boomerang is the control: WT_RETURNING makes it
# return after a hit, and WT_NO_MELEE ensures Fire must throw it. The subject is
# the Dwarven Thrower, whose WQ_RETURNING return is unconditional after a throw.
#
# RANGE AND FREEZE. Each goblin is summoned one square east, then the player
# walks four squares west. Freeze Monsters leaves the goblin behind, producing
# a five-square ranged shot instead of an adjacent melee swing.
#
# Run at seed 1 with INCURSION_OPTIONS=tools/gates/Options.Dat so Store Rolls in
# Log retains the hit and return messages for the final message-log dump.

# chargen.keys idiom, with its orc race choice replaced by a standard dwarf so
# the artifact keeps WQ_RETURNING when wielded.
a
n
y
@choose "Dwarf"
@choose "Dwarf (Standard)"
@choose "Barbarian"
a
@choose "Neutral"
a
a
RIGHT*3 DOWN RIGHT*3 DOWN RIGHT*3 DOWN RIGHT*3 DOWN RIGHT*3 DOWN RIGHT*3 DOWN
RIGHT*3 DOWN RIGHT*3 DOWN RIGHT*3 DOWN RIGHT*3 DOWN RIGHT*3 DOWN RIGHT*3 DOWN
ENTER y
y
RIGHT*3 DOWN RIGHT*3 DOWN RIGHT*3 DOWN RIGHT*3 DOWN RIGHT*3 DOWN RIGHT*3 DOWN
RIGHT*3 DOWN RIGHT*3 DOWN RIGHT*3 DOWN RIGHT*3 DOWN RIGHT*3 DOWN RIGHT*3 DOWN
ENTER y
@until "Afoot" ESC

# Confirm the early switch rows, then enable Auto-Identify Items (second row)
# before acquisition so the artifact arrives fully identified.
w
y
@choose "Wizard Mode Switches"
@dump:wizard-switches
DOWN
SPACE
ESC

# Freeze Monsters (eleventh Wizard Mode Switches row).
w
@choose "Wizard Mode Switches"
DOWN*10
SPACE
ESC

# Part A: acquire and wield the returning-by-type control weapon.
w
@choose "Item Acquisition"
RIGHT*9
@until "Boomerang" DOWN
DOWN
ENTER
2
ENTER
b
SPACE
n
s
ESC

# Fully identify the pack so weapon selection and dumps are unambiguous.
w
@choose "Identify Whole Pack"
i
ESC

# Summon the frozen control target adjacent, inspect the cave, then walk away.
w
@choose "Monster Summoning"
@choose "Goblinkin"
@choose "goblin"
RIGHT
ENTER
@dump:map-before-walk
LEFT
@while "Abort, Flee or Disengage" f
LEFT
@while "Abort, Flee or Disengage" f
LEFT
@while "Abort, Flee or Disengage" f
LEFT
@while "Abort, Flee or Disengage" f
@dump:ranged-setup

# Fire the boomerang five squares east and prove the return verb/setup.
f
a
RIGHT*5
ENTER
@while "Really fire" y
@until "returns to you" SPACE
@while "Wield the boomerang two-handed" n
@dump:boomerang-return-log

# Part B: acquire and wield the Dwarven Thrower.
w
@choose "Item Acquisition"
RIGHT*10
@until "Dwarven Thrower" DOWN
DOWN
ENTER
2
ENTER
b
SPACE
n
s
ESC
w
@choose "Identify Whole Pack"
i
ESC

# Use a fresh adjacent frozen goblin, then walk away to the same range.
w
@choose "Monster Summoning"
@choose "Goblinkin"
@choose "goblin"
RIGHT
ENTER
@dump:subject-map-before-walk
LEFT
@while "Abort, Flee or Disengage" f
LEFT
@while "Abort, Flee or Disengage" f
LEFT
@while "Abort, Flee or Disengage" f
LEFT
@while "Abort, Flee or Disengage" f
@dump:subject-ranged-setup

# Fire the wielded hammer at range, then record hand/ground state and the log.
f
a
RIGHT*5
ENTER
@while "Really fire" y
@dump:dwarven-thrower-after-throw
@while "two-handed" n
v
@dump:dwarven-thrower-return-log
ESC
@quit
